Phase 1 — drug–target affinity (`phase1/`, package `dti_gt`)
-----------------------------------------------------------
* GraphormerDTI (Gao et al., Comput. Biol. Med. 2024;
  https://github.com/mengmeng34/GraphormerDTI) — edge-aware graph transformer
  with bond-feature attention bias and Graphormer-style degree encoding.
  Re-implemented with PyTorch Geometric (no DGL).
* Dwivedi & Bresson, "A Generalization of Transformer Networks to Graphs"
  (AAAI Workshop 2021) and Ying et al., Graphormer (NeurIPS 2021).
* DeepDTA (Öztürk et al., Bioinformatics 2018) — 1-D CNN protein encoder and
  the MSE / CI / r_m² metric set.
* KIBA (Tang et al., J. Chem. Inf. Model. 2014) via Therapeutics Data Commons.
  The compact pair/drug/target tables in `phase1/data/kiba/` are a normalised
  copy of that public benchmark.
* ProtTrans / ProtBERT-BFD (Elnaggar et al., IEEE TPAMI 2021; Rostlab,
  MIT-licensed weights). The shipped `kiba_prot_bert_bfd.npz` is a 229 × 1024
  mean-pooled embedding table derived from those weights.

Phase 2 — medication recommendation (`phase2/`, package `hgdr`)
--------------------------------------------------------------
The official GRAND architecture (diagnose / genome / medication channels,
meta-paths P–D–P / P–M–P / M–P–M / M–G–M, semantic fusion, Dual-attention
Graph Transformer + InfoNCE) is documented in `phase2/docs/`. The released
`hgdr` model is the EHR+DDI subset that was actually trained (no genomes,
no InfoNCE DAGT head). See `phase2/README.md`.

* GAMENet (Shang et al., AAAI 2019) and SafeDrug (Yang et al., IJCAI 2021) —
  admission-level multi-label medication recommendation with a differentiable
  DDI-rate penalty; TWOSIDES top-40 side-effect convention.
* DRecHGR (DGL/HAN heterogeneous recommender used in the research notebooks) —
  P–D–P / P–M–P meta-path attention and Linear–Tanh–Linear semantic fusion.
  Approximated here by a PyTorch Geometric `HeteroConv` entity graph, not a
  1:1 HAN port.
* DrugDAGT (Chen et al., BMC Biology 2024) — dual-attention graph transformer
  with contrastive (InfoNCE) learning for pairwise DDI; used in the research
  notebooks and drawn on the official figure. Replaced in `hgdr` by a GAT/GIN
  molecular encoder plus a soft-DDI-rate loss.
* MIMIC-III v1.4 (Johnson et al., Sci. Data 2016) is **not** included.
  Access requires a PhysioNet credentialed Data Use Agreement and the data
  must not be redistributed. The public MIMIC-III demo is downloaded on demand
  by `phase2/scripts/demo_mode.ps1` and is never committed.
* TWOSIDES (Tatonetti et al., Sci. Transl. Med. 2012) — derived CID-pair table
  in `phase2/data/mappings/`.
* PubChem (Kim et al., Nucleic Acids Res. 2023) — name → CID → SMILES mapping
  in `phase2/data/mappings/`.

